  abstract = {This chapter is an introduction for biophysicists interested in the burgeoning field of systems immunology. We focus on recent development in T lymphocyte biology. First, we introduce the reader to three fundamental issues about immune responses that call for a quantitative understanding. Second, we review recent studies on T-cell activation that combines theoretical modeling and experimental work. Third, we present different models of T-cell proliferation. This review highlights how immunology benefits from more quantitative approaches (both experimentally and theoretically) and how the immune system is ideal to develop and test new concepts in systems biology.},
